== Attacks and abilities ==
Trolls come in two variants: 1/3rd of Trolls are equipped with a log, while the others are unarmed. 

Unarmed Trolls have three attacks.

=== Punch ===
Leans back before swinging to attack the player in a 5-meter 45-degree horizontal arc (60 [[Damage types#Blunt|Blunt]], 100 Tier 2 [[Damage types#Chop|Chop]] and 40 Tier 2 [[Damage types#Pickaxe|Pickaxe]] damage). This attack can be used every 4 seconds when within 4 meters of a player.

=== Ground slam ===
Lifts both fists up before slamming them down into the ground (70 [[Damage types#Blunt|Blunt]], 100 Tier 2 [[Damage types#Chop|Chop]] and 40 Tier 2 [[Damage types#Pickaxe|Pickaxe]] damage). This slam reaches 4.5 meters out in a 90-degree vertical arc, and can be used every 20 seconds when within 5 meters of a player. This effectively means that the Troll will punch five times before doing a slam, assuming that the player is always in range. When the slam hits anything, including the ground, it also creates a 3-meter area that deals 50 [[Damage types#Blunt|Blunt]], 50 Tier 2 [[Damage types#Chop|Chop]] and 30 Tier 2 [[Damage types#Pickaxe|Pickaxe]] damage. This area damage is the same at every star level.

=== Throw ===
Throws a large boulder at players within 8–20 meters (50 [[Damage types#Blunt|Blunt]], 60 Tier 0 [[Damage types#Chop|Chop]] and 40 Tier 0 [[Damage types#Pickaxe|Pickaxe]] damage). The boulder travels at an initial velocity of 15 meters per second and can travel for 4 seconds before disappearing. It has a spread of 10–20 degrees. This has a cooldown of 10 seconds and can be disabled by standing close to the Troll.

Log Trolls have two attacks.

=== Log swing (vertical) ===
Slams their log into the ground extending out 9 meters and spanning across 90 degrees (70 [[Damage types#Blunt|Blunt]], 100 Tier 2 [[Damage types#Chop|Chop]] and 40 Tier 2 [[Damage types#Pickaxe|Pickaxe]] damage). This attack can be used every 6 seconds when within 8 meters of a player.

=== Log swing (horizontal) ===
Swings their log from the side, creating a 10-meter 50-degree arc (60 [[Damage types#Blunt|Blunt]], 100 Tier 2 [[Damage types#Chop|Chop]] and 40 Tier 2 [[Damage types#Pickaxe|Pickaxe]] damage). This attack can be used every 6 seconds when within 8 meters of a player.

==Strategy==
{{For|strategies for defeating Trolls|Aggressive creature strategies#Troll}}
* Among the largest enemies in ''Valheim'', Trolls have a physical strength that reflects their size. Ranged attacks with a Bow or Spear are best and kiting a Troll through dense areas of the forest is very effective, as they have large hitboxes that hinder their pathfinding.
* Trolls employ massive yet slow attacks that are easy to avoid but very hard to block and parry. Using a [[Bone Tower Shield]] is effective at blocking most of its attacks, provided the player has sufficient health.
** "Pulling" the attention of a Troll and brandishing a tower shield while other players fire arrow volleys is an effective strategy.
* Trolls will sometimes fall into deep ditches or pits, or more often, the large pit at a copper dig site. Their poor pathfinding often renders them stuck.
** If a Troll approaches a ditch that is sufficiently deep (at least 6 meters) and does not fall in, it will not willingly walk in. Unable to reach the player, it will stand still, glowering into the pit. After a few moments, it will turn its aggression towards any player structures it can reach.
** Alternatively, if the positions are reversed, standing atop the ledge of a pit allows for easy dispatch with arrows and spears.
* Trolls can spawn with or without a tree trunk in their hand. A Troll equipped with a tree trunk has decidedly better range and destructive power than one that is not.

== Notes ==
* A 1-star Troll has a pale green tint, and a 2-star Troll is tinted a ruddy red.
* They are tall (7 meters) and can move along corridors 2 meters and wider.
* The curative pollen ejected by [[Greydwarf Shaman]]s also heals Trolls, as they share a [[Factions|Faction]].
* They cannot jump or swim, but they will walk along the bottom of shallow water, sometimes getting a considerable distance from the shore. They can walk through shallow water faster than a player can swim.
* All the Troll's attacks (except its rock throw) have a [[Damage#Terrain_damage|tool tier]] of 2, which allows players to use Trolls to harvest resources they are otherwise unable to attain at their current equipment level. Trolls are capable of knocking down and breaking apart [[Oak]] and [[Birch]] trees with their attacks, which is especially useful in the early game for obtaining [[Finewood]] without a [[Bronze Axe]] (or better). Trolls can also break [[Copper Deposit|Copper]] and [[Tin Deposit]]s (even with their rock throw attacks), which can allow the player to get [[Bronze]] before killing the first boss, [[Eikthyr]].
** Additionally, Trolls lured into more hostile biomes will aggressively attack most creatures in that biome, due to them having different Factions. While Trolls are not such a good match for stronger enemies, such as [[Plains]] creatures, they are capable of destroying large numbers of [[Swamp]] creatures, leaving loot like [[Entrails]] and [[Bloodbag]]s in their wake for the player to collect
* The [[Love Potion]] increases Troll spawn rate, star chances and alerts them.

